{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Water splash",
  "description": "A rock the size of two fists thrown into a pond from the bank, four metres away: the flat slap as it breaks the surface, the deep hollow \"gloop\" of the air pocket closing behind it at 60 ms (its pitch rising as the cavity shrinks), the hiss of the crown of water going up, and its droplets raining back from 200 to 900 ms, big ones first. Open air, a short reflection from the far bank.",
  "tags": [
    "nature",
    "water",
    "splash",
    "plunge",
    "pond",
    "dive",
    "impact",
    "liquid"
  ],
  "duration": "auto",
  "seed": 12,
  "tracks": [
    {
      "id": "slap",
      "note": "The first 30 ms: the surface breaking. A hard broad noise burst; it tells how flat and how fast the thing hit.",
      "source": {
        "type": "noise",
        "color": "white",
        "env": {
          "attack": 0.0006,
          "decay": 0.14
        },
        "filter": {
          "mode": "lowpass",
          "cutoff": [
            [
              0,
              9000
            ],
            [
              0.1,
              1500
            ]
          ],
          "q": 0.7
        }
      },
      "fx": [
        {
          "type": "transient",
          "attack": 3,
          "window": 0.006
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gloop",
      "note": "The cavity collapsing under water: a low resonant bubble at 150 to 400 Hz whose pitch climbs. The weight of the splash, in the range small speakers have.",
      "start": 0.058,
      "gain": -2,
      "source": {
        "type": "modal",
        "material": "rubber",
        "shape": "tube",
        "freq": [
          [
            0,
            135
          ],
          [
            0.08,
            190
          ],
          [
            0.22,
            420
          ]
        ],
